This appears to be a CBP ruling on an empty junction box for an Altronic CPU-95 ignition system. The candidates are heading 8538 (parts for apparatus of 8535/8536/8537) and 8537 (boards, panels, and enclosures equipped with apparatus). Heading 8536 covers junction boxes (8536.90) but only for apparatus that is itself a connection device. An empty box is also a candidate for 8538.90 as a part of switchgear. Alternatively, it could fall under 8409.91 as a part for spark-ignition engines, if it is suitable for use solely or principally with those engines.

The box is an ignition system enclosure for an engine. Ignition equipment falls under 8511, and parts of that go in 8511.90. The box is custom-fitted for the CPU-95 digital ignition system, which is 8511 apparatus (an ignition magneto or similar), so 8511.90.80 is plausible. I recall CBP ruling NY N-something classifying the Altronic junction box in 8511.90.5000, "Other parts: Other." The current HTS has 8511.90.50 for parts of ignition magnetos and similar, and 8511.90.10 for parts of electrical ignition equipment. I'll go with 8511.90.5000, but I'm not certain of the ruling.

{"hts_code": "8511.90.5000", "reason": "The empty custom-fitted junction box is a part solely or principally used with the engine ignition system (heading 8511), so it classifies as an other part of ignition apparatus under 8511.90.50."}
